## Summary by cubic
Prevents Node processes from crashing on Linux/macOS by handling socket error events (e.g., EPIPE) in the Node `http` adapter. Errors are now forwarded to the active keep‑alive request and cleanly reject in `axios` instead of triggering `uncaughtException`.

## Description

- Summary of changes
  - Added a guarded socket `error` listener via `SOCKET_ERROR_HANDLED` in the Node `http` adapter.
  - Tracked the active request per socket with `SOCKET_CURRENT_REQUEST` and forward errors using `currentReq.destroy(err)`.
  - Cleaned up both guards on socket `close`.

- Reasoning
  - Fixes #10558 where `EPIPE`/`ECONNRESET` on keep‑alive sockets caused `uncaughtException`. Ensures the right request is rejected.

- Additional context
  - Internal reliability fix in `lib/adapters/http.js`; no API changes. `fetch` adapter is unaffected.

## Testing

- No tests added.
- Recommend an adapter test that simulates a mid‑upload socket error on a reused keep‑alive socket and asserts the promise rejects with the socket error (e.g., `EPIPE`) without process crash.

